In the City of Baltimore, Maryland,
the State of Maryland has been the subject
of much discussion in the recent months. The
current state of the economy and the political
situation in the state has been a matter of
great interest to the people. The recent
election has resulted in a change of administration,
and the new government is expected to bring
about many changes in the state.

The recent election was held on the first Tuesday
in November, and the results were announced
on the following day.

The results of the election are as follows:
Governor, 15,000 votes;
Lieutenant Governor, 12,000 votes;
Secretary of State, 10,000 votes;
Comptroller, 8,000 votes;
Treasurer, 7,000 votes;
Attorney General, 6,000 votes;
Register of Wills, 5,000 votes;
Sheriff, 4,000 votes;
Clerk of the Court, 3,000 votes;
Coroner, 2,000 votes;
Jury Commissioner, 1,000 votes.

The election was held in all the counties of
the state, and the results were reported
to the Governor. The election was conducted
in a peaceful and orderly manner, and there
were no reports of violence or irregularities.

W. & N. Briefs must be sent to the editor.

Sine of the 2nd Logan, Baltimore.

